LOCATION:Grunwald Gallery
SUMMARY:BEYOND BOUNDARIES: Defying Genre Through Collaborative Creative P
 ractice
DESCRIPTION:Join IU alumni Anna Butterss (bassist/composer) and Josh John
 son (Grammy-winning saxophonist/producer) for a conversation on navigatin
 g cross-genre collaborations\, building versatile artistic careers\, and 
 transforming foundational IU training into a dynamic\, boundary-pushing c
 reative practice. This event is part of the November First Thursdays and 
 is co-hosted by IU Jazz Studies (Jacobs School of Music)\, IU Arts &amp\;
  Humanities Council\, and the Grunwald Gallery (Eskenazi School of Art\, 
 Architecture + Design).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join IU alumni Anna Butterss (bassist/c
 omposer) and Josh Johnson (Grammy-winning saxophonist/producer) for a con
 versation on navigating cross-genre collaborations\, building versatile a
 rtistic careers\, and transforming foundational IU training into a dynami
 c\, boundary-pushing creative practice. This event is part of the Novembe
 r First Thursdays and is co-hosted by IU Jazz Studies (Jacobs School of M
 usic)\, IU Arts &amp\; Humanities Council\, and the Grunwald Gallery (Esk
 enazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design).</p>
