X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20261106T010000Z
DTEND:20261106T020000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall
SUMMARY:Ingrid Matthews\, baroque violin
DESCRIPTION:Repertoire  J. S. Bach: Sonata in A Minor\, BWV 1003J. S. Bac
 h: Partita in D Minor\, BWV 1004About the ArtistIngrid Matthews teaches b
 aroque violin in the Historical Performance Institute at the Indiana Univ
 ersity Jacobs School of Music. She served previously as music director of
  the Seattle Baroque Orchestra and has appeared as a soloist\, guest dire
 ctor\, and concertmaster for leading early music ensembles including the 
 New York Collegium\, Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Musi
 c Festival Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra\, Musica
  Angelica\, The Bach Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroque Orchestra\, and many
  others. She is also a member of San Francisco-based chamber ensemble Mus
 ica Pacifica and has held teaching residencies at the University of South
 ern California\, University of Toronto\, Oberlin College\, Cornish Colleg
 e of the Arts\, New England Conservatory\, and others. First prizewinner 
 in the 1989 Erwin Bodky International Competition for Early Music\, Matth
 ews herself has served as a juror for competitions such as the Maurice an
 d Lillian Barbash International Bach Competition and the Indianapolis Ear
 ly Music Competition. She has received high critical acclaim for her exte
 nsive discography\; her recording of the Sonatas and Partitas for Unaccom
 panied Violin of J. S. Bach was named "top recommendation for this music 
 . . . on either period or modern instruments" by American Record Guide\, 
 and her recording of Biagio Marini is included in the Norton Anthology of
  Music used by conservatories and universities worldwide.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Repertoire</strong><br />  J. S. 
 Bach: <em>Sonata in A Minor\, BWV 1003<br /></em>J. S. Bach: <em>Partita 
 in D Minor\, BWV 1004<br /></em><br /><strong>About the Artist</strong><b
 r /><br /><strong>Ingrid Matthews</strong> teaches baroque violin in the 
 Historical Performance Institute at the Indiana University Jacobs School 
 of Music. She served previously as music director of the Seattle Baroque 
 Orchestra and has appeared as a soloist\, guest director\, and concertmas
 ter for leading early music ensembles including the New York Collegium\, 
 Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festival Orchestra\
 , Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra\, Musica Angelica\, The Bach 
 Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroque Orchestra\, and many others. She is also 
 a member of San Francisco-based chamber ensemble Musica Pacifica and has 
 held teaching residencies at the University of Southern California\, Univ
 ersity of Toronto\, Oberlin College\, Cornish College of the Arts\, New E
 ngland Conservatory\, and others. First prizewinner in the 1989 Erwin Bod
 ky International Competition for Early Music\, Matthews herself has serve
 d as a juror for competitions such as the Maurice and Lillian Barbash Int
 ernational Bach Competition and the Indianapolis Early Music Competition.
  She has received high critical acclaim for her extensive discography\; h
 er recording of the Sonatas and Partitas for Unaccompanied Violin of J. S
 . Bach was named "top recommendation for this music . . . on either perio
 d or modern instruments" by <em>American Record Guide</em>\, and her reco
 rding of Biagio Marini is included in the <em>Norton Anthology of Music</
 em> used by conservatories and universities worldwide.</p>
