DTSTART:20261113T000000Z
DTEND:20261113T010000Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
SUMMARY:New Art New Music
DESCRIPTION:An annual collaboration between the Student Composers Associa
 tion in the IU Jacobs School of Music and the Eskenazi School's Grunwald 
 Gallery. The performance will feature premieres by composers Sam Thompson
 \, Anchi Wang-Hall\, Devon Lee\, Archer Lohman\, and Darren Binkowski.  "
 STORY" is a creation myth drawn from the lived experience of the artist\,
  who was born and raised in Japan as a third-generation Korean national. 
 Infused with theatrical elements and embodied performance\, "STORY" explo
 res how one might establish a sense of self and live with rootedness amid
  the constant flux of identity.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1">  An annual collaboration betw
 een the Student Composers Association in the IU Jacobs School of Music an
 d the Eskenazi School's Grunwald Gallery. The performance will feature pr
 emieres by composers Sam Thompson\, Anchi Wang-Hall\, Devon Lee\, Archer 
 Lohman\, and Darren Binkowski.</p><p class="p1">  "STORY" is a creation m
 yth drawn from the lived experience of the artist\, who was born and rais
 ed in Japan as a third-generation Korean national. Infused with theatrica
 l elements and embodied performance\, "STORY" explores how one might esta
 blish a sense of self and live with rootedness amid the constant flux of 
 identity.</p>
